    "q-159818": {
      "dom_id": "step-q159818",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "Suppose ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{14}$ is an I.I.D random sample with ${X}_{i}∼B(6,\\theta )$ and unknown probability of success $\\theta .$ For a particular sample ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{14},$ you're given that \n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{14}{x}_{i}=24.\n$$\n\nFind the likelihood function of the sample up to a constant $C.$\n\n*Hint: The probability mass function for a binomial random variable is given by*\n\n$$\nf(x)=(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{n}{x}){\\theta }^{x}(1-\\theta )^{n-x},\\,x=0,1,2,…,n.\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that if ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{n}$ are independent and identically distributed discrete random variables with probability mass function $f(x;\\theta ),$ where $\\theta $ is an unknown parameter, then the likelihood function of a random sample ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}$ is\n\n$$\nL(\\theta )=P({X}_{1}={x}_{1},{X}_{2}={x}_{2},…,{X}_{n}={x}_{n})={\\prod }_{i=1}^{n}f({x}_{i};\\,\\theta ).\n$$\n\nIn our case, we are given a sample of $n=14$ independent binomial random variables with unknown probability of success $\\theta $ and $N=6$ trials, for which the probability mass function is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x;\\theta )=(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{6}{x}){\\theta }^{x}(1-\\theta )^{6-x}, & \\,x=0,1,2,…,6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can calculate the likelihood function as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(\\theta ) & ={\\prod }_{i=1}^{n}f({x}_{i};\\theta ) \\\\  & ={\\prod }_{i=1}^{n}(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{6}{{x}_{i}}){\\theta }^{{x}_{i}}(1-\\theta )^{6-{x}_{i}} \\\\  & =((\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{6}{{x}_{1}}){\\theta }^{{x}_{1}}(1-\\theta )^{6-{x}_{1}})\\cdot ((\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{6}{{x}_{2}}){\\theta }^{{x}_{2}}(1-\\theta )^{6-{x}_{2}})⋯((\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{6}{{x}_{n}}){\\theta }^{{x}_{n}}(1-\\theta )^{6-{x}_{n}}) \\\\  & =C\\,{\\theta }^{\\,\\sum {x}_{i}}(1-\\theta )^{\\,\\sum (6-{x}_{i})} \\\\  & =C\\,{\\theta }^{\\,\\sum {x}_{i}}(1-\\theta )^{\\,6n-\\sum {x}_{i}} \\\\  & =C\\,{\\theta }^{S}(1-\\theta )^{6n-S}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C={\\prod }_{i=1}^{n}(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{6}{{x}_{i}})$ is a constant and $S={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}.$\n\nWe are told that $S={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}=24$ and $n=14.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(\\theta ) & =C\\,{\\theta }^{24}(1-\\theta )^{6(14)-24} \\\\  & =C\\,{\\theta }^{24}(1-\\theta )^{60}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
